Gives the core a say over each file dialog a page opens: a file input's chooser, from
FileSelectHelper, and File System Access' pickers, which content asks Chrome's client for. Each
builds a ChromeSelectFilePolicy marked with which it is, whose CanOpenSelectFileDialog first asks
g_browser_core_page_file_dialog, a hook the core sets (//browser_core/hooks.h, #3656). Its false
keeps the dialog from opening, and SelectFileDialog then gives the page a cancel, as the
AllowFileSelectionDialogs policy's does, but without Chrome's infobar, as the core records the
refusal in its own activity log. The core refuses every page's dialog in an agent's tab the user
doesn't hold, where nobody watches what a dialog would hand the page. The browser's own dialogs,
as a download's Save As, aren't marked and aren't asked about.

